    "seconds": 24,
    "summary": "**Root cause:** The `productCatalogFailure` feature flag was set to `defaultVariant: \"on\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap. That flag makes the product-catalog service fail on a specific product.\n\n**Fix:**\n- I set `productCatalogFailure` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap.\n- I restarted `flagd` so it loads the new config, and restarted `product-catalog` so it picks up the flag change.\n- The ConfigMap now shows `\"off\"` and the `flagd` rollout finished. I did not re-check pod health or test product pages after the `product-catalog` restart.\n\nAll pods were Running before the change. The failure was in application behaviour, not in pod state.",
